# Visual verification

When a change alters user-visible behavior (panels, editors, Explore, query preview, copy/success feedback, remounting, layout):

## Required

- Capture a **screenshot**, a **short recording**, or both, showing **before** (broken) and **after** (fixed).
- Attach captures to the PR description and reference them from the ticket.
- Name the exact page, query, panel, or control shown so a reviewer can reproduce it.
- Prefer repo tooling:
  - Playwright e2e (`yarn e2e:playwright`) — screenshots and video
  - Local Grafana (`make run` + `yarn start`) exercised with browser tooling

## When visual capture is not feasible

Pure logic / non-UI paths, or UI that cannot run in this tree:

- Say so explicitly in the PR **Test plan** (**N/A — logic-only** or **N/A — UI not runnable here**).
- Still rely on automated tests (see `.cursor/rules/testing-coverage.mdc`).
- Briefly describe what a capture would have shown.

## Do not

- Ship UI-facing PRs with neither tests nor visual evidence.
- Include credentials, tokens, or real user data in any capture.
